// zerc-flags: --target-bits 32
// EXPECTED: compile error
// expect-error: accesses non-shared global
// A volatile global WIDER than the target word, written from a spawned thread.
//
// The volatile exclusion in the spawn global scan exists for the SINGLE-WORD
// volatile-flag idiom (see tests/zer/spawn_volatile_store_ok.zer, which stays
// allowed). The rationale is width-bounded; the check was not. On a 32-bit
// target a `volatile u64` store lowers to TWO 32-bit stores, so a concurrent
// reader can observe half of one write and half of another — a torn read the
// single-word argument never covered.
//
// Target-aware: the SAME program is accepted with --target-bits 64, where the
// store really is single-word. Use a shared struct or @atomic_* instead.
volatile u64 big;

void w(u32 a) { big = 5; }

u32 main() {
    spawn w(1);
    big = 0;
    return 0;
}
